{
  "name": "llm-advanced-det (the advanced panel of the LLM backend dialog: sampling parameters, HuggingFace autofill field, timeout, extra JSON, the two switches, cancelled without saving)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "Code-verified against components/settings/LlmBackendDialog.svelte + components/settings/llmBackendForm.ts + components/settings/SettingsToggle.svelte.",
    "llm-det opens this dialog and cancels it without ever expanding the advanced collapsible, so eleven controls behind llm-dialog-advanced-toggle had never been played.",
    "seedFrom(null) opens a new backend on provider llama-cpp, which is the branch that renders the HuggingFace autofill block; no provider change is needed to reach llm-dialog-hf-repo.",
    "Two controls are deliberately asserted present and never clicked, both because they leave the machine: llm-dialog-hf-fetch calls the HuggingFace API, and llm-dialog-test opens a connection to the backend endpoint. A deterministic run has neither, so clicking them would assert a network failure rather than a gesture. Same discipline as llm-det, which reduces the network actions to their boundary.",
    "llm-dialog-save is never clicked: the dialog is opened on the ADD path and cancelled, so the seeded three backends are left untouched and the script is re-runnable.",
    "The sampling fields are number inputs whose oninput reads valueAsNumber; the runner's fill dispatches a real input event, so the handler runs. llm-dialog-extra is a Textarea and is given valid JSON, because invalid JSON sets errors.extraJson and would only be visible on a save this script never performs.",
    "llm-dialog-enabled and llm-dialog-default are SettingsToggle wrappers, not inputs: the switch is the <button role=switch> the wrapper contains, which is what the runner's setChecked descends to. Both are driven AWAY from their seeded value first (enabled true, isDefault false), because setChecked only clicks on a mismatch and setting a field to the value it already holds is not a gesture.",
    "The advanced panel is collapsed again at the end and the collapse asserted by waitGone, so the toggle is exercised in both directions.",
    "The settings LLM panel is walked in builder mode, like llm-det and destructive.json: add-backend-btn and the per-card controls live in builder surfaces."
  ],
  "dynamicTestids": [
    "settings-nav-llm",
    "sidebar-mode-option-builder",
    "sidebar-mode-option-operator"
  ],
